cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tnkit: a backend-agnostic MPS/DMRG toolkit for GPU-accelerated tensor-network simulations"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tandon
    given-names: Aditya
    email: adityatandon29@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aditya-Tandon/tnkit"
abstract: >-
  tnkit implements DMRG, TDVP, TEBD, iDMRG, VUMPS and excited-state methods for
  matrix-product states behind a small backend interface, so the same kernel runs
  on numpy, torch-cpu, CUDA (cuSOLVER, double precision) and Apple MPS. The
  eigensolver is matrix-free and runs entirely on the device, which removes the
  host-device round trip per matvec that dominates host-driven DMRG at large bond
  dimension.
keywords:
  - tensor networks
  - matrix product states
  - DMRG
  - quantum many-body
  - GPU computing
# Keep these two together and in step with pyproject.toml's `version` on every tag.
version: 0.2.0rc2
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
